{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits","id":1374612,"title":"Vampires and Spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-13T12:24:32-07:00","id":1374612,"title":"Vampires and Spirits?","content":"I've been a little behind on Second Edition (loving it though!) and I was wondering if there were any bloodlines or subsets of Covenants that allow for vampires to deal with spirits rather than ghosts? I vaguely remember a non-Bloodline or Clan specific discipline in the Book of Spirits before but I didn't know if anything had been done since then or in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:44:13-07:00","id":1374618,"title":"","content":"It's not something vampires are especially adept at. The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp\" target=\"_blank\">Khaibit</a> have a couple Devotions which allow them to perceive and strike ephemeral entities, including spirits. The Tenth Choir's sacrileges, in Dark Eras 2, work to hunt and devour &quot;angels and devils,&quot; but this is defined broadly and includes &quot;appropriately biblical spirits.&quot; A while back I wrote a homebrew clan whose intent was to provide for more interaction between vampires and ephemeral entities, the Shiryo, which can be found in <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/file/7p5z0wrxgau56ve/Before_the_Bomb.pdf/file\" target=\"_blank\">this homebrew supplement</a>. Their clan Discipline was designed in part to be an alternate take on Blood Tenebrous, the Discipline from Book of Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T14:21:17-07:00","id":1374633,"title":"","content":"Blood Tenebrous has a fan update to second edition by one of the writers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854703\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T14:45:51-07:00","id":1374637,"title":"","content":"There's also <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263438/Spectral-Hunger?filters=0_0_45635_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">this supplement, Spectral Hunger</a>, which expands on interactions with ephemerals (mostly spirits and ghosts) and strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T18:26:57-07:00","id":1374679,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone! I remember the Khaibit but Stupid Loserman, your homebrew is way closer to what I was thinking. I like that update to Blood Tenebrous as well. And thanks nofather, I hadn't really checked out the Storyteller's Vault before and that opened up a whole new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T18:42:34-07:00","id":1375000,"title":"","content":"There's another Storytellers' Vault update to it in <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/265598/Ephemeral-Influence?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Ephemeral Influence</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T20:15:29-07:00","id":1375007,"title":"","content":"I am surprised that no one brought up how, while so far a 1st Edition feature, Cruac had rites for summoning and manipulating spirits, and that such wouldn't be hard to convert over to 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T22:42:21-07:00","id":1375016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits?p=1375000#post1375000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another Storytellers' Vault update to it in <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/265598/Ephemeral-Influence?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Ephemeral Influence</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great product, love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T11:33:56-07:00","id":1375306,"title":"","content":"For our game, I took the discipline of Blood Tenebrous and built a Mekhet bloodline around it. We actually spent a fair bit of time dealing with spiritual matters, since in our setting VII turned out to be half-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T08:53:20-07:00","id":1375438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits?p=1375007#post1375007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am surprised that no one brought up how, while so far a 1st Edition feature, Cruac had rites for summoning and manipulating spirits, and that such wouldn't be hard to convert over to 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always really liked this facet of the Circle from 1E and I still use it thematically now. While it's mostly flavor for me at this point (I'm still working on some Homebrew for Cruac), I'd always considered their practices and sorceries connected to, or at least sympathetic to, particular kinds of spirits. The Strix are the more obvious, and dangerous, higher spirits that could be summoned but for the vast majority of their spirit work, but certainly not the only variant. The vast majority of their arts could utilize lesser spirits, wisps of archetypal intention that occur in nature that are more bestial than sapient; think spirits of predation, hunger, and fear found in wilderness regions. Their cousins in cities would be more refined to human motives, but still as useful. <br /> <br /> Something like a blood drinking athame is formed through a compact, whether known or not, with a willingly bound lesser spirit of hunger or the hunt. The grounds where a Circle coven meets becomes a tainted nexus for these spirits, eventually allowing worshipers greater ease in the hunt or evading enemies. While they have nowhere near the knowledge of them that the Werewolves have, they still enjoy a primal, symbiotic connection to spirits by virtue of their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T04:18:07-07:00","id":1378969,"title":"","content":"I had thoughts about making Animalism/Auspex devotions that can effect spirits, the only one I can recall at the moment was three dots in each and let you convert Vitae to Essence and set a task for the spirit who accepts it, if they don\u2019t do the task they get a stage of blood bond, how this effects the spirits behaviour is dependent on the spirit, a fire spirit might have a hard time understanding that fuel doesn\u2019t think helping it burn is helpful and should actually be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T06:29:40-07:00","id":1378980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits?p=1378969#post1378969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had thoughts about making Animalism/Auspex devotions that can effect spirits, the only one I can recall at the moment was three dots in each and let you convert Vitae to Essence and set a task for the spirit who accepts it, if they don\u2019t do the task they get a stage of blood bond, how this effects the spirits behaviour is dependent on the spirit, a fire spirit might have a hard time understanding that fuel doesn\u2019t think helping it burn is helpful and should actually be avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or for something twisted, a homebrew merit for Animalism practitioners that infuses a point of Willpower per point of Vitae to give it sufficient potency to exist as Essence equivalent and allow levels 3-5 of Animalism to function on spirits in the effective ranges as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T08:12:00-07:00","id":1378988,"title":"","content":"Auspex has Spirits Touch so I saw that as the way to justify affecting spirits and animalism made the most sense as a way to get them to do what you want. I could see a bloodline that gets to use its disciplines on spirits as it\u2019s boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:22:10-07:00","id":1379001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits?p=1378988#post1378988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex has Spirits Touch so I saw that as the way to justify affecting spirits and animalism made the most sense as a way to get them to do what you want. I could see a bloodline that gets to use its disciplines on spirits as it\u2019s boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically most Disciplines would work equally well on ephemeral entities. The problem is the lack of vectors for interacting with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T11:16:36-07:00","id":1379022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1374612-vampires-and-spirits?p=1379001#post1379001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically most Disciplines would work equally well on ephemeral entities. The problem is the lack of vectors for interacting with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably part of why I chose Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T11:45:01-07:00","id":1379028,"title":"","content":"When I said most Disciplines, I actually meant all of them except for Animalism. But I do get the choice. It's about branching out Animalism to cover spirits, which feels very thematic. The easier (but less thematic way) would be to use an Auspex Devotion or Cr\u00faac Ritual to be able to see and hear spirits, and then just use Dominate and/or Majesty to their full effects (except possibly Possession).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}